  "packageSize": 166063,
  "published": "2025-11-07T18:49:07.14Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.2.0\nAdds multiple views,     TailwindANdDaisy,\n                         Custom,\n                         Plain,\n                         Bootstrap\nAdds plain CSS injection snippet. @Html.PlainCSS()\n0.3.0\nAdds light mode for all views.\n0.3.1 \nImproves layout for samples.\n0.3.2\nUpdates readme.\n0.5.0\nAdds the new FlippySortTagHelper to the package. This enables you to sort a list of items by clicking on the column headers.\n0.5.1\nUpdate this release notes as I forgot; update the Samples page.\n0.6.0\nThis update adds HTMX free capabilities to the FlippySortTagHelper. This means you can now sort a list of items without any JavaScript / HTMX.\n0.6.1\nFix to add an ability to return href plain when AutoAppend is set to false.\n0.6.2-0.6.3\nReadme updates.\n0.7.0\nNew functionality (in the Default Tailwind View) for preserving extra query parameters when paging.\n0.7.1\nAdd preserve query string params to page size dropdown.\n0.8.0-0.8.9\nUpdate PageSize to accept MaxPageSize, update query string logic to presrve query string params (client size). \nFix Table Sort to work properly with HTMX action links.\n\n0.9.0-0.9.2\nFix bug around totalitems being 0 and not showing the paging controls. Also fix client side bug to reset page to 1 when the page size changes.\n\n0.9.3\nShow page size even when there is no paging.\n\n0.9.4\nShow page size even when there is no paging.\n\n0.9.4.1\nSmall tweak to remove the daisyui select-primary class from the page size dropdown.\n\n1.0.0\nMAJOR UPDATE - Breaking changes and new features:\n\nNEW FEATURES:\n- ContinuationPager TagHelper: <continuation-pager> for NoSQL databases (Cosmos DB, DynamoDB, Azure Table Storage) that use continuation tokens instead of page numbers. Supports token history for backward navigation.\n- JavaScript Modes: New js-mode attribute with 5 options (HTMX, HTMXWithAlpine, Alpine, PlainJS, NoJS). Replaces use-htmx for better control.\n- Pure Tailwind View: New Tailwind view type using only Tailwind utilities (no DaisyUI dependency). TailwindAndDaisy view now fully exploits DaisyUI components.\n- NoJS View: Complete zero-JavaScript view using forms and standard links. Perfect for accessibility and progressive enhancement.\n- Localization: Built-in support for 8 languages (English, French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Japanese, Chinese). Use language attribute.\n- Custom Summary Templates: Customize pagination summary with placeholders: {currentPage}, {totalPages}, {totalItems}, {pageSize}, {startItem}, {endItem}.\n\nIMPROVEMENTS:\n- Updated to HTMX 2.0.4 (from 1.9.x)\n- Updated all NuGet dependencies (JetBrains.Annotations 2025.2.2, etc.)\n- Updated npm packages (DaisyUI 5.4.7, webpack 5.102.1, cssnano 7.1.2, cross-env 10.1.0)\n- Comprehensive documentation: Separate guides for each TagHelper, JavaScript modes, custom views, and getting started.\n- 106 passing unit tests\n\nBREAKING CHANGES:\n- use-htmx is deprecated (still works for backward compatibility). Use js-mode instead.\n- ViewType.TailwindAndDaisy now uses full DaisyUI components. For pure Tailwind, use ViewType.Tailwind.\n\nUSAGE:\nPager: <paging model=\"Model\" js-mode=\"HTMX\" />\nPageSize: <page-size model=\"Model\" />\nSortableHeader: <sortable-header column=\"Name\" current-order-by=\"@Model.OrderBy\" descending=\"@Model.Descending\">Name</sortable-header>\nContinuationPager: <continuation-pager model=\"Model\" />\n\nSee documentation at https://github.com/scottgal/mostlylucid.pagingtaghelper",
